**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`

**How to implement.** A fit's results, gathered, with each suspect entry's χ² profile (001 §L 'post-fit identifiability by profile likelihood for suspect parameters'; 001 §M workflow '6. post-fit identifiability'; the S11.4 brief 're-fit with the parameter stepped across its sigma range, and record the chi-squared profile' and 'Tests on synthetic studies: an identifiable pair against a confounded pair'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4. In `StudyEngine.fs`, after `realizabilityWith` (step 402): `type StagedStudy with member this.resultsWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) (data : StudyData) (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) (solution : StudyFitSolution) (watch : IterationWatch) : Result<FitRunResults, StudyFitError>`: the problems `engineProblemsWith` answers (step 402); `sigmas` their `sigmasFor solution.layout`; `problems` each one's `quality` (step 397), in order; their `runResiduals` and `productChecks`; `realizability` `realizabilityWith context solution.layout solution.fitted`; and `profiles`, for each of `suspectsWith this.study.settings.suspect solution.layout` in order, `{ entry; reasons; points }` of its problem's `profileAt coordinate earlier watch` (step 397), `earlier` the iterations of the profiles before it, so the profile pass counts its re-fits on from one through the fit's own watch. A `ProfileCancelledErr` answers `FitCancelledErr` (step 387) with its reason. A study whose thresholds flag nothing re-fits nothing, and nothing is written. No cache, retry or option is added. Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`, over test-local intensity studies made as step 387 makes its studies: items made by `ItemDraft` (step 216): a HeNe source item (`intensityScale`, step 207), a prep item of the ideal-LP preset at R1 0°, an analyzer item of the ideal-LP preset and an intensity-detector item (`gain`, `darkOffset`, step 208); one setup of the four, its slots built as `SetupTests` builds them; one Science run in one session, its gain model free, scanning the analyzer's `VaryR1` over nine readings; its points `IntensityData` answered by a test-local `ExperimentDataProxy`, point i being 2 · S₀ + 0.1 + 0.002 · (−1)ⁱ, S₀ the unit-scale intensity `ExperimentRun.read Intensity` gives at that reading (step 252); each study staged `JointStage` / `CalibrationHeldFixed` (step 385), fitted by `fitNonlinear` and its results taken by `resultsWith`, unwatched. `an identifiable pair is determined, with no suspect and no profile`: with `gain` unknown from 1.8 within [1, 4] and `darkOffset` unknown from 0 within [−1, 1], over the readings 0° to 160° by 20°: one problem of rank 2, both σ `Some` and below a tenth of their spans, their correlation −√(2/3) within 1e-6 (−Σuᵢ / √(n Σuᵢ²) for uᵢ = ½ cos² θᵢ), no suspect and no profile. `an exactly confounded pair has no sigma, and its profile is flat along the confounded direction`: with `gain` unknown from 1.8 within [1, 4], the source's `intensityScale` unknown from 1 within [0.25, 4] and `darkOffset` known at 0.1, over the same readings: rank 1, both σ `None`, no correlation, both entries suspect with `UndeterminedSigmaReason`; the gain's profile is seven points at 1, 1.5, …, 4, each `ProfileConverged` at the fit's χ² within 1e-9 relative (holding the gain, the scale takes up their product, which is all the data sees), and the scale's is seven points across [0.25, 4], each `ProfileConverged`. `a nearly confounded pair is suspect by its correlation and profiled across three sigmas`: with `gain` and `darkOffset` unknown as in `an identifiable pair is determined, with no suspect and no profile` over the readings 0° to 20° by 2.5°: rank 2 with a correlation beyond −0.95, each entry suspect with `CorrelatedEntryReason` naming the other, each profile seven points at x̂ + j · σ whose middle is the fit's χ² and whose χ² is χ²_min · (1 + j² / 7) within 1e-6 relative (a model linear in both, nine points and two parameters). `a profile pass under a cancelled watch answers FitCancelledErr`: `an exactly confounded pair has no sigma, and its profile is flat along the confounded direction`'s solution with `resultsWith` under a watch whose `CancellationTokenSource` is already cancelled answers `FitCancelledErr`. `a fit's results gather its sigmas, solves, run residuals, realizability and product checks`: over step 390's series fixture, under the thresholds `tryCreate 1.0 1.0e9`, the results hold one σ per entry, one problem per object solve, one run residual per fitted run, QZ's and LR's realizability, the [QZ; LR] product check and no profile.

**Acceptance.** After the profiles land, `StagedStudy.resultsWith` MUST gather the entries' σ, every solve's quality, every fitted run's residual, every black-box object's realizability, every series' product check and a χ² profile of every suspect entry by re-fits under the fit's watch, an identifiable pair yielding no profile and a confounded one flat profiles; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an identifiable pair is determined, with no suspect and no profile`, `an exactly confounded pair has no sigma, and its profile is flat along the confounded direction`, `a nearly confounded pair is suspect by its correlation and profiled across three sigmas`, `a profile pass under a cancelled watch answers FitCancelledErr` and `a fit's results gather its sigmas, solves, run residuals, realizability and product checks`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.
